cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this app, please cite it and the works it builds on, listed under references.
type: software
title: ecg-hrv
abstract: R-peaks, beat labels, heart rate and heart rate variability from the ECG of humans and animals, one step
  of the Cardiovascular Response to Nerve Stimulation and the Heart Rate Variability and Baroreflex workflows. R-peak
  detection with NeuroKit2 using species presets (human, pig, dog, rabbit, rat, mouse) for filter band, refractory
  period and heart-rate range, checked against WFDB XQRS; inverted-lead and mains handling; ectopic and artifact
  beat labels after Lipponen and Tarvainen 2019 as NeuroKit2 implements them; Task Force HRV (time domain, frequency
  domain with species bands, Poincare, DFA, sample entropy) over each recording and before, during and after each
  stimulation train; heart rate on a regular grid for dose-response analysis. Research outputs, not a clinical ECG
  interpretation.
authors:
- name: Pennsieve (University of Pennsylvania)
contact:
